   "stem_html": "In the 1912 U.S. presidential election, the Socialist Party",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1171804,
     "content_html": "gained the majority of its support from southern Democrats"
    },
    {
     "id": 1171803,
     "content_html": "sought to topple decades of Democratic presidential control"
    },
    {
     "id": 1171805,
     "content_html": "called for government nationalization of the major means of transportation and communication"
    },
    {
     "id": 1171802,
     "content_html": "supported the candidacy of William Jennings Bryan"
    }
